[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Shell Style Single Quotes
Comment=Taken from a real generated launcher. The Desktop Entry specification
Comment[x-note]=RESERVES the single quote and says it must not be used, so a strictly
Comment[x-note2]=spec-compliant tokenizer treats it as a literal character and splits
Comment[x-note3]='EMU Stuff' into two broken arguments. GLib's parser, which real
Comment[x-note4]=desktop environments use, honours it as shell-style quoting instead.
Comment[x-note5]=See CHECKLIST.md open issue OPEN-1. This fixture pins CURRENT
Comment[x-note6]=behaviour so that any future change is deliberate and visible.
Exec=flatpak run --command=bottles-cli com.usebottles.bottles run -p EzRO -b 'EMU Stuff' -- %u
Icon=single-quote
Terminal=false
